2026-06-22 22:51:02,223 | INFO | HTTP Request: POST http://127.0.0.1:11434/api/chat "HTTP/1.1 200 OK"
2026-06-22 22:51:02,224 | AGENT | SecurityCompliance Agent answered: Based on our company context at Faber IA, we can implement several security controls and compliance measures to address the requirements mentioned in the tender. 

To ensure GDPR compliance, we have already obtained ISO 27001 certification since 2023, which covers the scope of Development, delivery, and operations. Additionally, our ISO 27701 certification provides a privacy information management extension, demonstrating our ability to manage personal data in accordance with GDPR principles.

For encryption and pseudonymisation of sensitive data, we utilize encryption in transit via TLS 1.3 and encryption at rest using AES-256. Our key management is handled through EU-based infrastructure, ensuring that sensitive data is protected. We also implement strict partitioning of client files with logical isolation per client and per mission, preventing any cross-client circulation of data.

Regarding anti-money laundering obligations (LCB-FT), we are familiar with the framework and ensure that our solutions do not undermine a firm's reporting obligations. Our experience in working with clients bound by professional secrecy, including national professional orders, further demonstrates our ability to handle sensitive information while maintaining compliance with such regulations.

To maintain separation of duties and auditor's independence, we segregate duties between development and production operations. This ensures that no single individual has control over all aspects of the system, reducing the risk of data breaches or unauthorized modifications.

Compliance with legal retention and archival obligations for accounting documents is also ensured through our configurable retention policies, which are aligned with legal archival obligations. We maintain audit logging of access and every system output, providing a clear trail of activities performed on client data.

Our Data Protection Officer (DPO) appointment and maintenance of a data processing register further demonstrate our commitment to GDPR compliance and personal data protection. The availability of a Data Processing Agreement (DPA) aligned with GDPR Article 28 ensures that we can establish a contractual basis for the processing of personal data on behalf of clients.

Overall, our existing security controls and compliance measures provide a solid foundation for addressing the requirements outlined in the tender, ensuring the confidentiality, integrity, and availability of client data while maintaining strict compliance with relevant regulations.
